<!--Validator Style Check — PreferOmitUnusedNamespace
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.compiler.validator.style.PreferOmitUnusedNamespace-->
<valstyle:PreferOmitUnusedNamespace xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:valstyle="org.blockml.bml.compiler.validator.style">

  <baseType>
    valstyle:StyleCheck
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Warn when a root xmlns prefix is never used
  </is>
  <documentation>
    <![CDATA[
    Matches a document-root xmlns:<prefix> binding whose prefix is never used as a
    type QName, annotation namespace, or xsi schemaLocation host.

    The default xmlns is never unused. Implicit documentation language (default
    English) and see relation= local names (SeeAlso, ReadNext, …) do not count —
    they resolve to org.blockml.bml.language / org.blockml.bml.relation without an
    authored QName. An ancestor package prefix such as blockml (org.blockml.bml)
    is used only when a type or language element is actually written with that
    prefix.

    Nested bindings must not steal credit. xmlns:ann="org.blockml.bml.annotation"
    plus xmlns:bml="org.blockml.bml.annotation.BmlAnnotation" is the usual pair:
    <ann:BmlAnnotation /> uses ann (package + local name), not bml. A type-level
    xmlns is used only for that prefix as a QName (bml:version, bml:id, …) or when
    a bml:* field was parsed off the attribute. Resolving a parent-prefix QName to
    the same FQN is not a use of the nested prefix.

    Style warning only — does not fail ValidateResult.success.
    ]]>
  </documentation>
</valstyle:PreferOmitUnusedNamespace>
